  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 1234 PM MDT Sat Sep 5 2026\n\nHeading into next week, the upper tough will move east through the \nGreat Basin, sending some shortwave energy into our region. This \nwill coincide with the monsoon plume and allow for some greater \ncoverage for showers/storms on Monday. Most activity will be over \nand near the higher terrain, while the eastern plains remain hot and \nlargely dry.\n\nThat low moves off to the northeast by midweek, leaving an uncertain \npattern for the rest of this forecast period. Long-range guidance \nsuggests the presence of a system off the west coast, while keeping \nhigh pressure in place over our area. Beyond that, the behavior and \nevolution of the synoptic pattern varies greatly between models and \nruns. Overall, daily showers and storms will likely continue for our \nmountains due to lingering moisture. Storms will be slow-moving \nbeneath the lighter winds, so we may see an uptick in flash flooding \nconcerns. Meanwhile, temperatures are expected to decrease a few \ndegrees, closer to seasonal averages.",
